        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Cnoc Na Sonas,1 Ballycurran Demesne, Headford, Co. Galway, H91X2C2, is a truly magnificent five-bedroom detached residence that epitomizes standard-setting lakeshore living. \r\n\r\nNestled on the scenic Galway-Mayo border, the property is situated within an ultra-private, secluded cul-de-sac composed of fewer than ten select homes, allowing it to enjoy an idyllic sense of privacy while maintaining a warm, welcoming neighborhood community feel. Positioned directly on the pristine shores of Lough Corrib, this unique home boasts a spectacular private entrance and a dedicated, scenic walkway that leads directly from your doorstep down to the banks of the water. This private pathway offers an unrepeatable lifestyle, allowing you to wander down for a morning swim, launch a kayak, or enjoy an evening stroll straight to the water's edge to appreciate the uninterrupted, world-class natural beauty of the loch. \r\n\r\nThe exterior of the property is a masterclass in traditional craftsmanship and curated landscaping, reflecting the immense love, care, and attention to detail poured into it by the current owners. The residence itself features a striking, timeless natural cut-stone facade, approached by a sweeping gravel driveway and framed by exceptionally large, beautifully manicured rolling lawns and vibrant floral borders. The expansive grounds seamlessly connect the home to its aquatic backdrop, with the private walkway cutting a peaceful route through the greenery down to the shoreline, effectively transforming the banks of the loch into an extension of your own garden. Tucked within the grounds is a bespoke, artistic metal fire pit sculpture celebrating the home's identity as \"Cnoc na Sonas.\" Practical storage and hobby needs are effortlessly met by an extraordinarily large detached steel garage, specifically engineered with an extra-high roller door configuration to seamlessly accommodate a large mobile home, caravan, or substantial lake boat. \r\n\r\nAdditionally, a gorgeous, deep-set paved veranda runs alongside the stone exterior of the house, sheltered by a transparent-roofed timber pergola with hanging plants, providing an exquisite all-weather outdoor sanctuary for dining and entertaining while overlooking the pristine gardens. \r\n\r\nInside, the property continues to impress with its highly stylish, soul-infused interior design choices that blend rustic warmth with modern comfort. The heart of the home is a wonderfully authentic country-style kitchen, complete with extensive solid oak cabinetry, premium integrated appliances, a multi-tiered tiled splashback, and a distinctive, heavy-top curved wooden central island that acts as a natural gathering point. Terracotta floor tiles lead past a beautiful half-split stable door that opens directly out to the veranda. This space flows effortlessly into a sprawling, light-filled open-plan dining and living area. This grand reception room is anchored by a floor-to-ceiling feature stone fireplace housing a cozy solid fuel stove, beautifully complemented by warm wood flooring, tongue-and-groove timber-paneled ceilings, and elegant French doors that flood the room with natural light and lead out to the gardens. \r\n\r\nThe sleeping and private quarters are distributed across a generous and versatile layout, offering five beautifully proportioned bedrooms that cater perfectly to family living or executive remote working. A handsome staircase leads to a character-rich upper landing, which has been cleverly utilized to create a sunlit reading nook or home office study station, illuminated by a large overhead Velux window and framed by floor-to-ceiling custom bookshelves. \r\n\r\nEvery corner of Sonas feels intentional, warm, and immaculately maintained, making it a rare and deeply special market offering where the tranquility of the countryside meets the ultimate private access to the shores of Lough Corrib."
      },
